From f07ae12789b5fea64c9afa18a593ce5dc4798c0a Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Ian Blenke <ian@blenke.com>
Date: Wed, 17 Jun 2026 23:10:14 -0400
Subject: [PATCH 02453/11362] [outer-loop] best-first live explorer (opt-in):
 cheap value head collapses it -> capacity is the limit

Operator: take on the best-first live-explorer refactor (the cn04 unlock came from graph_explore's
BEST-FIRST search; the live StepwiseExplorer is depth-first-ride). Added an opt-in search_mode=
"best_first" (default "depth_first_ride" unchanged) that always expands the globally-best A*-value
frontier, + a --policy explorer_bf eval mode. Measured live with the v2 head at weight 5.

RESULT: best_first + v2 head + weight 5 = 0/32 (TOTAL COLLAPSE -- loses even the easy BFS wins; the
weak head routes the search into dead-ends and it explores out early, e.g. lp85 gave up in 336
actions, r11l in 2890). cn04 did NOT transfer (its graph_explore unlock was implementation-specific).

CONCLUSIVE -- the cheap cross-game LINEAR value head cannot route the live search. Full space mapped:
  baseline BFS                                     8/32
  v1 (5feat)  override / tiebreak                  3 / 8
  v2 (41feat) A*-nudge (depth-first-ride)          6
  v2 (41feat) best-first DRIVER                    0
The MORE control the head gets over search order, the WORSE -- the head is actively MISLEADING, not
merely weak. The search STRUCTURE (best-first) was the right idea; the value-model CAPACITY is the
binding constraint live.

REFINED NEXT LEVERS (the honest payoff of mapping the cheap space):
  1. a REAL learned value model -- TRM / grid-embedding CNN with capacity + much more data (the
     linear-on-features head is fundamentally insufficient to DRIVE a search). The TRM slot, a GPU
     build, fed by the now-built offline solve corpus.
  2. STRONGER world-model induction -- bigger proposer / RFT on our banked solves (deep games).

SAFE STATE: submitted agent unchanged -- pure BFS 8/32 (value_head=None, value_weight=0,
search_mode=depth_first_ride defaults). All value-routing + best-first are OPT-IN via the eval.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 4.8 <noreply@anthropic.com>
